      {
        "id": 246195,
        "name": "",
        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-07-10T15:28:44.701Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Here’s some evidence to the contrary: the description for the Overlord Villain Archetype reads, “Count the number of minions and lieutenants loyal to the Overlord in the scene to determine their current status.” Then under that Archetype’s Status heading, it reads,</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>9+ minions: <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/2/27110002319772281a5e8f68eb5b373db7e914f5.png?v=12\" title=\":d12:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":d12:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><br>\n5-8 minions: <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/2/25f0d022a48321f60d425e1534e706ee824a4b1b.png?v=12\" title=\":d10:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":d10:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><br>\n3-4 minions: <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/3/329c72e5b8e6369e1b922b98850b5d1a68931335.png?v=12\" title=\":d8:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":d8:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><br>\n1-2 minions: <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/0/0d92f02a3c6f83672e750fc4564408b6ef178bbd.png?v=12\" title=\":d6:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":d6:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><br>\n0 minions: <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/8/81f6971826a4b7fd3e8e99b5b756f5045f94cb75.png?v=12\" title=\":d4:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":d4:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This seems to imply that “minions” (in the Status section) refers to both Minions and Lieutenants (as specified in the description).</p>\n<p>This could, of course, simply be a one-time thing, wherein “minions” means “both Minions and Lieutenants.” What do you all think?</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-07-10T15:28:44.701Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 30,
        "readers_count": 29,
        "score": 31.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 29465,
        "topic_slug": "do-lieutenants-count-as-minions",
        "display_username": "",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": "Regular",
        "title_is_group": false,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "Here’s some evidence to the contrary: the description for the Overlord Villain Archetype reads, “Count the number of minions and lieutenants loyal to the Overlord in the scene to determine their current status.” Then under that Archetype’s Status heading, it reads,\n\n> 9+ minions: :d12:\n> 5-8 minions: :d10:\n> 3-4 minions: :d8:\n> 1-2 minions: :d6:\n> 0 minions: :d4:\n\nThis seems to imply that “minions” (in the Status section) refers to both Minions and Lieutenants (as specified in the description).\n\nThis could, of course, simply be a one-time thing, wherein “minions” means “both Minions and Lieutenants.” What do you all think?",
